# Silent Night
artist: Franz Xaver Gruber, 1818 — public domain
key: B
notation: H
tempo: 44
time: 6/8
capo: 3

// The key is B flat: in H-notation "B" is B flat and "H" is B natural.
// Guitar plays capo 3 and reads G shapes; keys read the sounding chords
// and have their own, fuller part in the verses.

## Intro
| F7 | B | B*** F7*** | B |
@keys > solo: melody of the last line, one octave up
@guitar > let the first chord ring, enter with picking in bar 3

## Verse 1
| B | | F7 | B |
| Eb | B | Eb | B |
| F7 | B | B*** F7*** | B |
@keys | B | Bsus4 B | F7 | B |
@keys | Eb | B/D | Eb | B/D |
@keys | F7/C | B/D | B/F*** F7*** | B |
@bass > enter in line 2
@vocals > in unison, the melody
> first line: guitar and voice only
Silent night, holy night
All is calm, all is bright
Round yon virgin mother and child
Holy infant so tender and mild
Sleep in heavenly peace
Sleep in heavenly peace

## Verse 2 = Verse 1
@drums > brushes, start here
@alto > a third below the melody from line 3
Silent night, holy night
Shepherds quake at the sight
Glories stream from heaven afar
Heavenly hosts sing Alleluia
Christ the Saviour is born
Christ the Saviour is born

## Interlude = Intro

## Verse 3 [quiet]
| B | | F7 | B |
| Eb | B | Eb | B |
| N.C. | | B F7 | B | rit.
@keys > pads only, no left hand
> line 3: voices alone for two bars
@soprano > descant on the last line
@alto > hold the last note with the soprano
Silent night, holy night
Son of God, love's pure light
Radiant beams from Thy holy face
With the dawn of redeeming grace
Jesus, Lord, at Thy birth
Jesus, Lord, at Thy birth

## Outro x2
| Eb | B |
